{
  "executive_summary": "E2E Driver ran a focused 16-minute mathematics lesson on proper fractions with clear sequence and multiple concrete models; lesson-plan fidelity (B) is the strongest area. Highest-growth need is in classroom feedback practice — specific, actionable feedback was mostly absent, reducing chances to correct and extend student thinking. Teacher reflected that pacing largely worked and said they will give quieter students more time to answer next time, which supports implementing quick, high-impact changes to wait-time and participation norms.",
